WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
1633.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.080
A voice stands up and
argues with Death itself:

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:10.050
"Death, be not proud, though
some have callèd thee".

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.730
1848.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.750
A lone voice confesses a fear: "When
I have fears that I may cease to be".

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.560
1855.

7
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.080
A voice in an empty
room longs for the dead:

8
00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.150
"O that 'twere possible".

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.610
Same subject.

10
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.570
So why do these three poets
sound centuries apart?

11
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.060
In this mission, you'll
meet three movements,

12
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:38.700
Metaphysical, Romantic and Victorian,
and ask what labels like that are worth.

13
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.960
You'll follow Donne's argument with Death,

14
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.840
and stand with Keats on the shore, alone.

15
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.730
And you'll hear Tennyson's speaker
ask where the dead have gone.

16
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.520
Your mission: explain why
they sound centuries apart.
